WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.780
- It's time for Drew's News,

00:00:01.780 --> 00:00:05.750
the only news with the portable
desk, including a mess.

00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:09.700
And with me at the traveling
desk is my trusty co-pilot,

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:12.667
and just one of the loves of
my life, "Rossi" Ross Matthew.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.699
- Hi, hi everybody!

00:00:14.699 --> 00:00:16.020
(audience cheers)

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:19.447
- And this season, our motto
is, "have desk will travel".

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.410
As you can see, Ross and I are taking

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:25.010
our little news show on the
road all across America,

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:27.970
and I'm thrilled to kick it
off right here in my hometown,

00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:30.870
right in front of the
Hollywood sign, I mean,

00:00:30.870 --> 00:00:32.050
how crazy is that?

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.050
- See I love this, Drew,

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:34.780
you know, I thought we
had fun in season one,

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.850
now we are on the road,

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.650
so watch out America, we're coming.

00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:40.870
- We'll be doing this all season long,

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.480
so, if you want the desk in your hometown,

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:47.750
we would like you to reach
out to us and let us know.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:50.250
Send us a message on
social media and tell us

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.680
where the desk should go next.

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.730
- Maybe we'll be in your town, watch out.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.030
- Okay, so for the last month

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.847
everyone's been asking one big question,

00:01:00.847 --> 00:01:04.980
"splish, splash, should
we be taking less baths?"

00:01:04.980 --> 00:01:06.360
Vogue reports that it's the

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.950
latest trend in Hollywood hygiene,

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.780
Ashton Kutcher and Mila Kunis
say that they only bathe

00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:14.890
themselves and their
kids when they see dirt.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:18.830
Dax Shepard and Kristen
Bell say their family

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:21.189
waits until they smell the stink!

00:01:21.189 --> 00:01:23.330
- [Ross] Ugh, Oh!

00:01:23.330 --> 00:01:27.407
- And Jake Gyllenhaal says he
barely showers because quote,

00:01:27.407 --> 00:01:29.350
"we naturally clean ourselves"

00:01:29.350 --> 00:01:31.539
and you know the ladies are like, "okay".

00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:33.328
(audience laughs)

00:01:33.328 --> 00:01:38.210
Ross, "to bathe or not to
bathe", that is the question,

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.230
what do you think?

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:40.380
- Do what you want,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.630
if you want to save it
until you smell the stink

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:45.860
before you bathe, good for
you, but not Ross Matthews.

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.000
I don't play like that.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.990
I don't know, like I just feel like I

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:52.153
can't be my best self unless
I smell artificially clean.

00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:56.010
- What do you guys think, raise your hand

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:58.480
if you think that you don't

00:01:58.480 --> 00:02:01.130
really need showers all the time.

00:02:01.130 --> 00:02:02.380
- [Ross] Thank you!

00:02:02.380 --> 00:02:03.520
(audience laughs)

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:04.370
Thank you!

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.450
- And by the way, I mean,

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:09.780
we have to acknowledge
the fact that someone

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:12.760
I am the biggest fan of,

00:02:12.760 --> 00:02:13.920
Seth,

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.050
mister dude with sign.

00:02:16.050 --> 00:02:19.550
I want to know, do you
have any bread crumbs

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:21.980
of a trail that traces back

00:02:21.980 --> 00:02:26.010
to kind of how this really
started, Dude with sign

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.090
that now has 8 million
followers basically?

00:02:29.090 --> 00:02:33.570
- Yes, so, basically I was
working for a card game company

00:02:33.570 --> 00:02:35.790
and I was writing just like funny jokes,

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.530
and we were also trying to do

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.730
funny content every day just for fun.

00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:41.557
And one day we tried one that said,

00:02:41.557 --> 00:02:44.053
"stop replying all" to
company-wide emails.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.080
We were, we were emailing and
it was someone's birthday.

00:02:47.080 --> 00:02:48.777
And then everyone was replying
all those things like,

00:02:48.777 --> 00:02:50.200
"oh my God, happy birthday, Jenna",

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:51.830
like it was just really annoying,

00:02:51.830 --> 00:02:53.490
and we were like, "oh, we
should go protest this,

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.323
Seth, you'll do it",

00:02:54.323 --> 00:02:56.030
and I was like, "I'll do it",

00:02:56.030 --> 00:02:56.863
went out there and did it

00:02:56.863 --> 00:02:58.610
and it blew up, everyone really liked it,

00:02:58.610 --> 00:02:59.443
and I was just kinda like,

00:02:59.443 --> 00:03:01.260
"we could probably keep doing this".

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.690
Yeah, it definitely worked out.

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:05.700
- And then you're hanging
out with Justin Bieber-

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:07.262
- [Seth] And Drew Barrymore, what's up?

00:03:07.262 --> 00:03:08.153
- Oh, my god!

00:03:08.153 --> 00:03:09.330
(Ross and audience laugh)

00:03:09.330 --> 00:03:11.410
You also were just at the white house

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:12.243
in the Oval
- [Seth] Yeah.

00:03:12.243 --> 00:03:13.500
- [Drew] Office with Biden.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:14.333
- [Seth] Yes.

00:03:14.333 --> 00:03:17.260
- All right, next step,
one of Hollywood's finest,

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:18.350
Christopher Maloney,

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:20.430
you know him, and recently he,

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.760
he was on the cover of Men's Health

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:25.210
looking like a total "Zaddy" at age 60,

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.210
he's 60 years old you guys,

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.700
but now the New York Post reports,

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:31.920
dictionary.com's just
added the word "Zaddy",

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.330
and it's defined as "An attractive
man who is also charming

00:03:35.330 --> 00:03:37.831
and self-confident" and if you look it up,

00:03:37.831 --> 00:03:39.180
my picture's right there.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.084
No, it's not!

00:03:40.084 --> 00:03:40.917
(Drew and audience laugh)

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:42.900
Chris Maloney says now that
he knows what it means,

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:45.940
he is happy to be America's zaddy.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:48.707
Look at this zaddy, Chris Maloney.

00:03:48.707 --> 00:03:50.320
- [Drew] Oh my gosh.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:51.160
- All right, well, next up,

00:03:51.160 --> 00:03:53.840
apparently it's not just Jen and Ben

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:55.360
who are getting back together.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:58.560
A new relationship study
says many people hook up

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:00.600
with their exes, and you know what,

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:02.770
women, I didn't mean to point at you,

00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:03.711
women...

00:04:03.711 --> 00:04:04.684
(Ross laughs)

00:04:04.684 --> 00:04:05.517
- Oh, we've all,

00:04:05.517 --> 00:04:06.400
oh I've got around the bend with the exes,

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:08.190
of course, that's what we do.
- I was gonna ask you.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:12.010
- It's 'cause you're convinced
that it's unrequited,

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:14.410
maybe you've changed,
maybe it's unfinished,

00:04:14.410 --> 00:04:15.243
Anyway, keep going.

00:04:15.243 --> 00:04:17.610
- Well women, women do
it more than men do,

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.980
and it sounds like you
are one of them, yeah.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.140
Uh, Women and Homes says the study found

00:04:22.140 --> 00:04:25.680
that 54% of women had slept with an ex,

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:29.140
while only 14% of them actually
wanted to get back together,

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:32.003
they were like, "I quit it,
but I can still hit it",

00:04:32.003 --> 00:04:32.836
you know?

00:04:32.836 --> 00:04:33.669
(audience laughs)

00:04:33.669 --> 00:04:35.947
Well, Dude with the
sign, what do you think?

00:04:35.947 --> 00:04:38.170
(Drew and audience laugh)

00:04:38.170 --> 00:04:40.400
- And yet you can never tell
them because guess what,

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:43.325
the second they get back
together, you're in the doghouse.

00:04:43.325 --> 00:04:44.790
- Yeah, mhmm.

00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:47.463
- Now, this story is
my favorite of the day.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.500
We've got some really great
news for students and families

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:53.270
right here in California.

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:56.170
CNN is reporting that
the state is offering

00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:00.540
universal free lunch to all public school

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:02.315
students this fall.

00:05:02.315 --> 00:05:04.320
(everyone applauds)

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:09.140
Nearly 60% of the students
qualify for free lunch

00:05:09.140 --> 00:05:12.470
or reduced lunch, but this
year, thanks to the work

00:05:12.470 --> 00:05:15.210
of over 200 organizations,

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.770
every student will get a
balanced, nutritious lunch,

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:21.750
free of charge and free of stigma.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:26.460
California is the very first
state to get this done.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:28.700
Not only am I so in awe of this,

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:32.154
I want to know how we can
take this across our country.

00:05:32.154 --> 00:05:32.987
- Yes!

00:05:32.987 --> 00:05:35.500
- California, thank you
for setting the bar.

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:40.314
May we all follow in your
footsteps and example.

00:05:40.314 --> 00:05:43.647
(rousing, upbeat music)

